WHAT IS EXCEPTION?:
An Exception is an unexpected and unwanted event that occurs during program execution and disturbs the normal flow of the program.(Program terminates abnormally)
Example:
---------
int a = 10/0;   // ArithmeticException

Graceful Termination: Program ends successfully.
Abnormal Termination: Program terminates in the middle due to exception.
Purpose of Exception Handling: To achieve graceful termination of the program.

Benefits:
1. Prevent abnormal termination.
2. Maintain normal program flow.
3. Improve application reliability.
4. Handle runtime problems gracefully.

