catch BLOCK: Used to handle exceptions occurring in try block.
-----------
-If Exception occur in try block then only catch block will execute, otherwise catch block will not execute.
try {
    // risky code
}
catch(Exception e) {
    // handling code
}

Example:
---------
try {
    String s = null;
    System.out.println(s.length());
}
catch(Exception e) {
    System.out.println("Handled");
}

