------
int i = 10;
Integer obj = new Integer(i);
System.out.println(obj);       //10

AUTO BOXING (Java 5): Automatic conversion of primitive type into wrapper object.
--------------------
int i = 10;
Integer obj = i;          // Auto Boxing
System.out.println(obj);  //10

Internally:  Integer obj = Integer.valueOf(i);

UNBOXING: Converting a Wrapper Object into primitive data type is called Unboxing.
---------
Integer obj = new Integer(10);
int i = obj;
System.out.println(i);         //10

5. AUTO UNBOXING (Java 5): Automatic conversion of Wrapper Object into primitive type.
--------------------------
Integer obj = 100;
int i = obj;      // Auto Unboxing
System.out.println(i);   //100

Internally: int i = obj.intValue();


